WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Your flight moves. Your hotel, ride and dinner don't move with it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Maya's parents shift from Friday to Saturday morning; the guest count rises from two to three.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The browser connects to the self-hosted MCP server, initializes, and lists seven tools.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The server proposes seven operations. Sunday departure stays fixed, and existing commitments remain unchanged.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:52.000
I review only the arrival-day restaurant cancellation and its simulated $75 fee.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:06.000
I approve that exact operation. Approval changes no commitment; execution is still pending.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:20.000
I execute separately. One cancellation completes, while the other six proposals await decisions.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:32.000
The browser briefly shows the actual initialize, tools/list, and tools/call request/response evidence.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:52.000
The server ends with six live commitments, six open decisions, and one simulated $75 sunk fee.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
The $329 of $300 figure includes pending proposals; it is not completed spend. All services and fees are fictional.
